TC03: LUMAX CHIPYARD 1.13.0
START: 2026-10-09T21:45:54.206931+03:00
PLANNED: 72 independent simulator invocations. Input16, weights8/4/2, RIN=1, six designs.
Each design built once with make and reused across every TC; Python generates/checks integer references only.
No HW logic edits. Config.scala geometry is temporarily selected during the six initial builds and restored immediately after each.
No dimension padding. DMA-readable buffers have nonzero guard bytes; output guards begin immediately after the logical output.
Packed bytes use ceiling allocation for fractional-byte tails; unused packed bits are nonzero.
TC11 uses six operations in one RISC-V ELF/Verilator boot, with shared buffers and no accelerator reset.
Full X/W printed for up to 2048 weights; larger matrices include seeds and hashes, plus every Python/HW output.
